# Phase 4 — Interview simulation

This is probably the most important phase.

I'll start asking you questions like an interviewer:

> **"Walk me through your payment flow."**

Then:

> "Why did you use MongoDB?"

> "How do you prevent duplicate payments?"

> "What happens if two requests arrive simultaneously?"

> "Why isn't your application-level idempotency check sufficient?"

> "What happens if the PSP times out?"

> "Would you retry a payment?"

> "What happens if the PSP processed the payment but your service didn't receive the response?"

> "How would you reconcile it?"

> "Why CompletableFuture?"

> "How do you size your thread pool?"

> "What happens when the thread pool is exhausted?"

> "Why Kafka?"

> "How do you guarantee exactly-once payment processing?"

> "How do you handle Kafka consumer failure?"

> "What happens if Mongo goes down?"

These are the questions that connect **Java + Spring + async + Kafka + DB + payment domain**.

That's exactly the kind of preparation we want.

